# One person, several spellings, one address. Git history carries "DCJ" and a
# personal name against jack@dotcomjack.com, so `git shortlog -sn` reports two
# contributors and the Swift Package Index would headline the acronym as the
# author of a security library.
#
# Canonicalised to DotcomJack, which is the same author string the application
# repository publishes. Two public repositories crediting the same person under
# two different names is a small thing that reads as carelessness.
#
# Because every spelling shares one commit address, the single name form is
# enough. The two address mapping form is not needed here.
DotcomJack <jack@dotcomjack.com>
